-- title:
--   Weighted zonotopes $Z_t$ generated by matrix rows, and Minkowski subtraction $K\ominus L$
-- statement:
--   Let $A\in\mathbb R^{m\times n}$ have rows $a_1,\dots,a_m\in\mathbb R^n$. For $t\in\mathbb R^m_{\ge0}$ the **weighted zonotope** is
--   $$Z_t=\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^m y_i a_i:\ |y_i|\le t_i\ \text{for all } i\in[m]\Big\},$$
--   the Minkowski sum of the segments $t_i[-a_i,a_i]$; the zonotope generated by the rows of $A$ is $Z=Z_{\mathbf 1}$. Repeated or zero rows and every rank are allowed, so $Z$ need not be full dimensional.
--
--   For sets $K,L\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ the **Minkowski subtraction** is
--   $$K\ominus L=\{x\in\mathbb R^n:\ x+L\subseteq K\}.$$
--   It is the actual set, possibly empty; it is not a formal inverse of Minkowski addition, and $(K\ominus L)+L\subseteq K$ can be strict.
--
--   These are the objects of every statement of the mission: the support function of $Z_w$ is $u\mapsto\sum_i w_i|\langle a_i,u\rangle|$, which links the zonotope inclusions $(1-\varepsilon)Z\subseteq Z_w\subseteq(1+\varepsilon)Z$ to $\ell_1$ row sparsification.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Points of $\mathbb R^n$ are functions `Fin n → ℝ` and the row $a_i$ is `A i`. `zonotope A t` is the literal set for every `t`; the statements use it only with `t ≥ 0` (for $x\in[-1,1]^m$, $\mathbf 1+x\ge0$). The source defines $K\ominus L$ for compact convex $K,L$ with $L$ nonempty; the formula is the same, and every subtrahend used here (a segment or a zonotope with nonnegative weights) is nonempty.
-- source:
--   Victor Reis, Thomas Rothvoss, Linear-size ℓ1 sparsifiers, STOC 2027 submission #162 (October 2026; PDF SHA-256 5137e7dee3cd303bd508f90f5f42c955632af5dc2ec978d9ef575bae4ce23710), §1.2, p.4 ($Z$, $Z_t$); Definition 13, p.7; §3.2, p.8

import Mathlib

namespace L1Sparsifiers.Main

open scoped Pointwise

/-- **Weighted zonotope generated by the rows of a matrix.**
Reis–Rothvoss, *Linear-size ℓ1 sparsifiers*, STOC 2027 submission #162, §1.2, p.4 and §3.2, p.8:
for `A ∈ ℝ^{m×n}` with rows `a₁,…,a_m` and `t ∈ ℝ^m_{≥0}`,
`Z_t = { ∑ᵢ yᵢ aᵢ : |yᵢ| ≤ tᵢ ∀ i ∈ [m] }`, and `Z = Z_𝟏` is the zonotope generated by the rows.

The row `aᵢ` is `A i : Fin n → ℝ`. Repeated or zero rows and every rank are allowed. The
definition is the literal set for every `t`; it is used only with `t ≥ 0`. -/
def zonotope {m n : ℕ} (A : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) ℝ) (t : Fin m → ℝ) : Set (Fin n → ℝ) :=
  {z | ∃ y : Fin m → ℝ, (∀ i, |y i| ≤ t i) ∧ z = ∑ i, y i • A i}

/-- **Minkowski subtraction** (Definition 13, p.7): `K ⊖ L = {x : x + L ⊆ K}`.
This is the actual set (it may be empty); the source uses it for compact convex `K, L` with `L`
nonempty, and every application below has a nonempty subtrahend. -/
def minkowskiSub {n : ℕ} (K L : Set (Fin n → ℝ)) : Set (Fin n → ℝ) :=
  {x | ∀ y ∈ L, x + y ∈ K}

end L1Sparsifiers.Main


